IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`
IMPORT `sfaa-div1-interpretation`
IMPORT `sfaa-div1-directors`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Layer 1, Part 7 Division 1 Subdivision (2): disclosure by substantial shareholders (sections 135, 136, 137, 137A and 137B).
-- Who is a "substantial shareholder" is section 2(6) (the keel); here it is a fact asked of the caller. "Corporation" is the listed body of section 130(2).
-- The 2-business-day limits are counted by sfa-periods.l4 (P8); "becomes aware" is read with section 130(6) (the earlier of the actual day and the day reasonable
-- diligence would have given awareness). A notice given on or before the last day is in time (fork register A3).

§ `s 135: duty of a substantial shareholder to notify the corporation of interests`

-- src:28348 | 135.—(1) A person who is or (if the person has ceased to be one)
-- src:28349 | had been a substantial shareholder in a corporation must give written
-- src:28350 | notice to the corporation of particulars of the voting shares in the
-- src:28351 | corporation in which the person has or had an interest or interests and
-- src:28352 | the nature and extent of that interest or those interests.
@ref s 135(1) (src:28348-28352)
GIVEN
    `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies (the answer to the question under section 130(2): a listed company, or a corporation with a primary listing)?
    `the person is a substantial shareholder in the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a substantial shareholder in the corporation (as section 2(6) defines it)?
    `the person had been a substantial shareholder in the corporation but has ceased to be one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the person been a substantial shareholder in the corporation, and has the person since ceased to be one?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 135(1) the person must give the corporation written notice of particulars of the voting shares` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a substantial shareholder in a corporation"; the body is not a corporation as section 130(2) reads the word for Division 1
        IF `the person is a substantial shareholder in the corporation` OR `the person had been a substantial shareholder in the corporation but has ceased to be one`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is or (if the person has ceased to be one) had been a substantial shareholder in a corporation must give written notice"

-- src:28358 | (a) must be in such form and must contain such information as
-- src:28359 | the Authority may prescribe;
@ref s 135(2)(a) (src:28358-28359)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has prescribed the form and the information for the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed a form for the notice and the information it must contain?
    `the notice is in the form the Authority prescribes and contains the information it prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice in the form the Authority has prescribed, and does it contain the information the Authority has prescribed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 135(2)(a) the notice is in the form and contains the information the Authority prescribes` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Authority has prescribed the form and the information for the notice`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "as the Authority may prescribe"
        IF `the notice is in the form the Authority prescribes and contains the information it prescribes`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be in such form and must contain such information as the Authority may prescribe"

-- src:28361 | (b) must be given within 2 business days after the person
-- src:28362 | becomes aware that the person is or (if the person has
-- src:28363 | ceased to be one) had been a substantial shareholder; and
@ref s 135(2)(b) (src:28361-28363)
GIVEN
    `the day the person actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person actually become aware of the fact or occurrence?
    `the earliest day on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` IS A DATE @desc What is the earliest date on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager as the case may be, would have become aware of the fact or occurrence if acting with reasonable diligence in the conduct of their affairs?
    `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which dates in the period were there public holidays in Singapore? (Saturdays and Sundays are counted automatically.)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 135(2)(b) the last day for the notice` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a number of business days after` (`s 130(6) the day from which the person is taken to have been aware` `the day the person actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` `the earliest day on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence`) 2 `the public holidays`

@ref s 135(2)(b) (src:28361-28363)
GIVEN
    `the day the person actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person actually become aware of the fact or occurrence?
    `the earliest day on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` IS A DATE @desc What is the earliest date on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager as the case may be, would have become aware of the fact or occurrence if acting with reasonable diligence in the conduct of their affairs?
    `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given?
    `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which dates in the period were there public holidays in Singapore? (Saturdays and Sundays are counted automatically.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 135(2)(b) the notice is given in time` MEANS
    IF `the day the notice is given` AT MOST `s 135(2)(b) the last day for the notice` `the day the person actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` `the earliest day on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` `the public holidays`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be given within 2 business days after the person becomes aware"; a period fixed in the text's own words (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (a))

-- src:28368 | (c) must be given even though the person has ceased to be a
-- src:28369 | substantial shareholder before the expiration of the period
-- src:28370 | referred to in paragraph (b).
@ref s 135(2)(c) (src:28368-28370)
GIVEN
    `the person has ceased to be a substantial shareholder before the end of the period for the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person ceased to be a substantial shareholder before the end of the 2 business days allowed for the notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 135(2)(c) the notice must be given although the person has ceased to be a substantial shareholder within the period` MEANS
    IF `the person has ceased to be a substantial shareholder before the end of the period for the notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must be given even though the person has ceased to be a substantial shareholder before the expiration of the period"; a person who has not ceased is under paragraph (b) alone

DECLARE `s 135 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 135 give the corporation written notice`

-- src:28348 | 135.—(1) A person who is or (if the person has ceased to be one)
-- src:28349 | had been a substantial shareholder in a corporation must give written
-- src:28350 | notice to the corporation of particulars of the voting shares in the
-- src:28351 | corporation in which the person has or had an interest or interests and
-- src:28352 | the nature and extent of that interest or those interests.
-- src:28356 | (2) A notice under subsection (1) —
-- src:28358 | (a) must be in such form and must contain such information as
-- src:28359 | the Authority may prescribe;
-- src:28361 | (b) must be given within 2 business days after the person
-- src:28362 | becomes aware that the person is or (if the person has
-- src:28363 | ceased to be one) had been a substantial shareholder; and
@ref s 135(1) and (2)(b) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:28348-28363)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 135 action`
`s 135(1) and (2)(b) the substantial shareholder must give written notice within 2 business days` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    MUST `s 135 give the corporation written notice`
    WITHIN 2
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "written notice was not given to the corporation within 2 business days after the person became aware (section 135(2)(b))"

§ `s 136: duty of a substantial shareholder to notify the corporation of a change in interests`

-- Subsection (3): the "percentage level": votes attached to the voting shares the person has an interest in, as a percentage of the votes attached to all the voting shares
-- (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation or, where the share capital has 2 or more classes, in the class concerned, rounded DOWN to a whole number.
-- Fork register A4: the numerator is read as written ("all the voting shares in which the substantial shareholder has an interest"), whatever the class.
-- src:28390 | (3) In subsection (1), “percentage level”, in relation to a substantial
-- src:28391 | shareholder in a corporation, means the percentage figure ascertained
-- src:28392 | by expressing the total votes attached to all the voting shares in which
-- src:28393 | the substantial shareholder has an interest or interests immediately
-- src:28394 | before or (as the case may be) immediately after the relevant time, as
-- src:28395 | a percentage of the total votes attached to —
-- src:28397 | (a) all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the
-- src:28398 | corporation; or
-- src:28400 | (b) where the share capital of the corporation is divided into
-- src:28401 | 2 or more classes of shares, all the voting shares (excluding
-- src:28402 | treasury shares) in the class concerned,
-- src:28404 | and, if it is not a whole number, rounding that figure down to the next
-- src:28405 | whole number.
@ref s 136(3) (src:28390-28405)
GIVEN
    `the total votes attached to all the voting shares in which the substantial shareholder has an interest or interests` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes in total are attached to all the voting shares in which the substantial shareholder has an interest or interests, immediately before or after the relevant time?
    `the share capital of the corporation is divided into 2 or more classes of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the share capital of the corporation divided into two or more classes of shares?
    `the total votes attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes in total are attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation?
    `the total votes attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the class concerned` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes in total are attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the class concerned (leave 0 if the corporation has one class)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 136(3) the percentage level of the substantial shareholder's interests` MEANS
    IF (IF `the share capital of the corporation is divided into 2 or more classes of shares` THEN `the total votes attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the class concerned` ELSE `the total votes attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation`) AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE FLOOR ((`the total votes attached to all the voting shares in which the substantial shareholder has an interest or interests` TIMES 100) DIVIDED BY (IF `the share capital of the corporation is divided into 2 or more classes of shares` THEN `the total votes attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the class concerned` ELSE `the total votes attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation`))

-- Subsection (1) opens with "Where there is a change in the percentage level": a "where" condition, so with no change the answer is JUST FALSE (periods ruling of 2026-11-05,
-- rule (b)); the duty falls on a substantial shareholder, so a person who is not one is outside it (NOTHING).
-- src:28377 | 136.—(1) Where there is a change in the percentage level of the
-- src:28378 | interest or interests of a substantial shareholder in a corporation in
-- src:28379 | voting shares in the corporation, the substantial shareholder must give
-- src:28380 | written notice to the corporation within 2 business days after the
-- src:28381 | substantial shareholder becomes aware of the change.
@ref s 136(1) (src:28377-28381)
GIVEN
    `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies (the answer to the question under section 130(2): a listed company, or a corporation with a primary listing)?
    `the person is a substantial shareholder in the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a substantial shareholder in the corporation (as section 2(6) defines it)?
    `the percentage level of the interests before the change` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the percentage level (a whole number) of the substantial shareholder's interests in the voting shares immediately before the change?
    `the percentage level of the interests after the change` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the percentage level (a whole number) of the substantial shareholder's interests in the voting shares immediately after the change?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 136(1) the substantial shareholder must give the corporation written notice of the change in the percentage level` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a substantial shareholder in a corporation"; the body is not a corporation as section 130(2) reads the word for Division 1
        IF NOT `the person is a substantial shareholder in the corporation`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the substantial shareholder must give written notice"
        IF `the percentage level of the interests before the change` EQUALS `the percentage level of the interests after the change`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where there is a change in the percentage level of the interest or interests of a substantial shareholder"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

