§ `s 137A: the beneficial owner must ensure notification by the person who holds, acquires or disposes of interests on the owner's behalf`

-- "Where a person (A) authorises another person (B) ...": a "where" condition, so without the authority the answer is JUST FALSE (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b)).
-- src:28431 | 137A. Where a person (A) authorises another person (B) to hold,
-- src:28432 | acquire or dispose of, on A’s behalf, voting shares or an interest or
-- src:28433 | interests in voting shares in a corporation, A must take reasonable
-- src:28434 | steps to ensure that B notifies A as soon as practicable and, in any
-- src:28435 | case, no later than 2 business days after any acquisition or disposal of
-- src:28436 | any of those voting shares or interest or interests in voting shares
-- src:28437 | effected by B on A’s behalf which will or may give rise to any duty on
-- src:28438 | the part of A to give notice under this Subdivision.
@ref s 137A (src:28431-28438)
GIVEN
    `the person has authorised another person to hold, acquire or dispose of voting shares, or an interest in voting shares, in the corporation on the person's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person authorised another person to hold, acquire or dispose of, on the person's behalf, voting shares or an interest in voting shares in the corporation?
    `the other person has effected an acquisition or disposal on the person's behalf that will or may give rise to a duty to give notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the other person effected, on the person's behalf, an acquisition or disposal of any of those voting shares or interests that will or may give rise to a duty on the person to give notice under this Subdivision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137A the person must take reasonable steps to ensure that the other person notifies the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person has authorised another person to hold, acquire or dispose of voting shares, or an interest in voting shares, in the corporation on the person's behalf`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person (A) authorises another person (B) to hold, acquire or dispose of, on A's behalf, voting shares or an interest or interests in voting shares in a corporation"
        IF `the other person has effected an acquisition or disposal on the person's behalf that will or may give rise to a duty to give notice`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty attaches to "any acquisition or disposal ... effected by B on A's behalf which will or may give rise to any duty on the part of A to give notice"; none has occurred

-- Whether the steps taken were "reasonable" is a judgment the text does not define: it is a plain input (the person's own account of what was done).
-- src:28431 | 137A. Where a person (A) authorises another person (B) to hold,
-- src:28432 | acquire or dispose of, on A’s behalf, voting shares or an interest or
-- src:28433 | interests in voting shares in a corporation, A must take reasonable
-- src:28434 | steps to ensure that B notifies A as soon as practicable and, in any
-- src:28435 | case, no later than 2 business days after any acquisition or disposal of
-- src:28436 | any of those voting shares or interest or interests in voting shares
-- src:28437 | effected by B on A’s behalf which will or may give rise to any duty on
-- src:28438 | the part of A to give notice under this Subdivision.
@ref 2 s 137A (the steps) (src:28431-28438)
GIVEN
    `the person has taken reasonable steps to ensure that the other person gives notice as soon as practicable and within 2 business days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person taken reasonable steps to ensure that the other person notifies the person as soon as practicable and, in any case, within 2 business days after the acquisition or disposal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137A the person has taken reasonable steps` MEANS
